=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported fault — "sshswitch SVIs for VLAN 5 and VLAN 6 are down" — is not present in the live lab. Both Layer-3 bridge interfaces on sshswitch (`br_v5` at 10.5.0.254/24 and `br_v6` at 10.6.0.254/24) are fully operational: each shows operstate `UP/LOWER_UP`, carries the correct /24 address, and responds to ICMP from access-VLAN hosts with 0% packet loss and sub-millisecond RTT.

Inter-VLAN routing through sshswitch is also confirmed healthy — every VLAN 5 host reaches every VLAN 6 host at 0% loss via these SVIs, which would be impossible if either SVI were down.

The broader infrastructure is equally clean: infra_sweep found no ACL drops, no addressing divergence, and all 15 access hosts hold valid IPs with functioning default routes; ospf_snapshot confirms all nine FRR routers are up with Full adjacencies and 18 OSPF routes each; pressure_sweep found no resource stress on any device; l2_snapshot found no duplicate MACs.

The STALE ARP entries for 10.5.0.254 visible on VLAN 5 hosts are normal kernel behaviour: they indicate no recent traffic to the gateway, but the entries remain valid and are revalidated on the next use — not a fault indicator.

No flap script, carrier-change history, or daemon anomaly was found to explain even a past transient outage. The helpdesk report is unconfirmed by any live or historical evidence.

Root cause: No anomaly exists — the sshswitch SVIs (br_v5 and br_v6) are UP with correct addresses and are actively routing.

Fix: No corrective action required; the infrastructure is functioning as designed.
=== END ===